            <ArticleTitle>[Psychosomatics of the success of operations in intervertebral disk lesion patients].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>53-66</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>With surgeries of the lumbar disks a comparatively high quota of failures has been found. Therefore, referred to patients who had repeatedly undergone ineffective surgery, the hypothesis was stated that psychosomatic reasons account for this small surgical success.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
